@@ -3 +3,10 @@
-const REVIEW_GUIDANCE = `Review protocol: before reviewing a worker's result, freeze taskId, reviewId, named reviewer provider/model, scope, criteria and maxRounds with leerness review-feedback start --stdin. For a first and a final reviewer, freeze ordered stages instead (v2 schema, each with its reviewer and maxRounds): only the stage that gave NO GO re-reviews, and the next stage starts after it passes. Keep ordinary work within 3 rounds across all stages (maxRounds 3, or stages of 2 and 1): the full frozen scope first, then the reported findings and their regressions, then a final check. A spent budget is never GO; open blockers stop as NEEDS_DECISION. Reuse the reviewId; never restart to reset its budget. A new stage starts in a new session (reviewerSession), never one used by another stage or by the implementation; the same model may serve several stages, and a re-review in the same stage may continue its session. For a repair re-review, give the reviewer leerness review-feedback show REVIEW-ID --brief, the diff since the reviewed revision and actual test results. For a fresh independent final-stage reviewer, supply frozen requirements, exact target/base commit, affected code and actual test evidence without prior reviewer verdicts, findings, or developer self-assessment until the cold inspection is recorded; reconcile after that. A review ID restores no conversation memory. A re-review checks only the open finding IDs, that diff, the call paths it affects, related regression tests, the fixed criteria and real new regressions or serious risks, widening only where the change reached a new module or data boundary. Submit with leerness review-feedback submit --stdin. The final response itself must include a TO_GO section for every NO GO/FAIL, written as a numbered checklist in fix order: for each open blocking issue its ID, affected file/component/behavior, evidence and how to reproduce it, why it fails, the required changed behavior, and each observable acceptance check with how it will be verified and the evidence needed for GO; then the fixed criteria and regression check still pending, the reviews left and the next steps. Never return only a verdict or point to a separate log; apply the same format when reviewing without the CLI. Say GO for PASS; for FAIL or NEEDS_DECISION say NO GO and which kind: fix required, verification pending, decision pending, or tool error, which is never a product defect by itself. Structured verdicts remain PASS, FAIL and NEEDS_DECISION; an unrun check is unverified. Each finding requires ISSUE, EVIDENCE, WHY_IT_FAILS, REQUIRED_OUTCOME and ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA; IMPLEMENTATION_HINT is optional and the worker chooses the implementation. A mandatory constraint needs a security, data-loss, API-contract or standards reason and evidence. Preferences, UX ideas and out-of-scope requests are non-blocking follow-ups; only a new regression with before/after evidence adds a blocker. Severity alone does not make a medium finding non-blocking, and rarity does not lower real data-loss risk. A pre-existing defect found after the first round that breaks a frozen criterion is a medium-or-higher risk-escalation that stops for a decision, not an inflated severity or a regression. PASS requires every fixed criterion and the regression check to pass with no open blocker. Add a regression test for a reproduced defect, reuse adequate tests, keep mutation testing for critical boundaries of uncertain detection, run one source through one check, and never weaken a failing security or data-integrity test. On NEEDS_DECISION stop automatic revisions and report open issues, evidence and required decisions. With an explicit owner instruction and an eligible result.nextResumeTemplate from show --json, record one re-review decision with leerness review-feedback resume --file <decision file>; NO GO and the remaining budget stay. If the installed tool lacks resume or reports a tool/ledger error, report a tooling blocker and continue independent product work. Do not switch to modifying the verification tool, reset review IDs, update shared installations or stop other projects unless explicitly requested; never auto-pass or silently change the baseline. References and identity declarations are not verified execution or release approval.`;
+const REVIEW_COVERAGE_INSTRUCTIONS = Object.freeze([
+  "For initial and independent reviews, complete one bounded pass over the frozen scope and directly affected call and storage boundaries. Inspect the pinned source and add missing in-scope cases; the implementer checklist is not proof of completeness.",
+  "For stateful changes, enumerate applicable transitions and event orders: absent/A/B/absent/A identity changes, loading/success/failure, late or cancelled responses, retries, repeated effects, submission during reload or lock, and concurrent clients. Trace the same invariant through state, request payload and server persistence; justify cases that do not apply.",
+  "Do not stop safe inspection at the first blocking finding. Report ALL blocking findings found in this pass together with their IDs, evidence, reproduction, required outcome and acceptance checks; keep non-blocking notes separate. Never claim that every possible defect has been found.",
+  "For each checklist row, record its criterion or invariant, status (checked, issue-found, unverified or not-applicable), file:line or execution evidence, and whether it was inspected statically or tested. Checked does not mean test PASS; an unrun required check stays unverified. A reference alone is not verified coverage.",
+  "For rechecks, continue the same stage session where available and supply prior finding IDs, the previous revision, the diff and actual test results. Revisit affected transitions and relevant previously unverified rows, not unrelated whole-project searches. A fresh independent final review receives no earlier conclusions before its cold findings are recorded.",
+  "Respect the frozen budget, access rights and safe execution boundary. If time, context, missing inputs, unsafe execution or record limits prevent completion, report inspected and remaining scope and the reason; do not silently truncate, reset review IDs or infer PASS. Apply length limits to the summary, preserving complete findings in a referenced detailed report.",
