l error, which is never a product defect by itself. Structured verdicts remain PASS, FAIL and NEEDS_DECISION; an unrun check is unverified. Each finding requires ISSUE, EVIDENCE, WHY_IT_FAILS, REQUIRED_OUTCOME and ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA; IMPLEMENTATION_HINT is optional and the worker chooses the implementation. A mandatory constraint needs a security, data-loss, API-contract or standards reason and evidence. Preferences, UX ideas and out-of-scope requests are non-blocking follow-ups; only a new regression with before/after evidence adds a blocker. Judge blocking by the service's documented normal range: a display-only defect that needs an unrealistic value (a billion-item consumer order) is a low non-blocking note; money, stock, data, overflow, input, auth and crash risks still block. If the range is undocumented, ask the user one question per decision and use NEEDS_DECISION. Severity alone does not make a medium finding non-blocking, and rarity does not lower real data-loss risk. A pre-existing defect found after the first round that breaks a frozen criterion is a medium-or-higher risk-escalation that stops for a decision, not an inflated severity or a regression. PASS requires every fixed criterion and the regression check to pass with no open blocker. Add a regression test for a reproduced defect, reuse adequate tests, keep mutation testing for critical boundaries of uncertain detection, run one source through one check, and never weaken a failing security or data-integrity test. On NEEDS_DECISION stop automatic revisions and report open issues, evidence and required decisions. With an explicit owner instruction and an eligible result.nextResumeTemplate from show --json, record one re-review decision with leerness review-feedback resume --file <decision file>; NO GO and the remaining budget stay. If the installed tool lacks resume or reports a tool/ledger error, report a tooling blocker and continue independent product work. Do not switch to modifying the verification tool, reset review IDs, update shared installations or stop other projects unless explicitly requested; never auto-pass or silently change the baseline. References and identity declarations are not verified execution or release approval.`;
